<%# The drawer as the dashboard's frame sees it: the panel and nothing else. A full-page
    visit to this URL does not render this template -- TargetsController#show renders the
    dashboard instead, with the drawer already open inside it -- because a bare overlay
    has nothing behind it, and closing it would empty the only element on the page. %>
<%# refresh: "morph" is repeated here so that a frame filled by the ⋯ keeps morphing on
    reload; Turbo carries the attribute over from whichever element it renders.

    No src, deliberately: this template *is* the response to fetching that URL, and Turbo
    refuses a frame whose src points at the request it arrived in ("has a source URL which
    references itself"), leaving the drawer empty. The requesting frame already knows its
    own src -- either Turbo set it navigating here, or projects/show rendered it. %>
<%= turbo_frame_tag "drawer", refresh: "morph" do %>
  <%= render "targets/drawer", project: @project, target: @target %>
<% end %>
